A reset executed inside the APDU handler lands BEFORE the response is
transmitted (apdu_finish runs after cmd_initialize returns) — measured
as Transmit failed on the host for every initialize. The old
watchdog_reboot(0,0,500) masked this by being asynchronous; the
synchronous busy-wait + SYSRESETREQ replacement exposed it, and
SYSRESETREQ itself turned out to reset only the asserting core on this
silicon. Schedule the reset instead: return now, response goes out,
card_watchdog_task() fires it from core0's loop 500ms later via the
bootrom's rom_reboot() (see the submodule commit).
